{
 "meta": {
  "schema": "gs-site-args/v1",
  "semantics": "Virtual-dispatch site argument evidence, direct-to-GS (bypasses the occupant equivalence chain). At each `push argK; ...; mov ecx, recv; call [vtreg+off]` site (full_export disasm snapshot), up to nstk(slot-family stack-arg count from slot_param_groups) pushes are collected by a backward scan (stops at call/ret/j*/label/esp-adjust); push nearest the call is k=0 (k = stack-arg index, this excluded, identical to GS k convention). Each push operand is def-traced (<=10 insns, <=2 reg copy hops; call defines caller-saved: eax=>EAX entity, edx/ecx=>unclassified): gs-str: push offset <string> (string_literals-verified) => char* family; gs-const: push <numeric imm> (image-VA-range values excluded as address evidence) => int family; gs-pdirect: mov reg,[ebp+arg_N]/[ebp+X] (function input param, k=N/4 or (X-8)/4, fn-arity guarded) => equivalence GS == P:FN:origK; gs-eax: push <eax or copy thereof defined by a preceding call> (RETX-A window discipline) => equivalence GS == EAX:FN:producer_call_site; gs-slot: mov reg,[ebp+var_X] => GS == S:FN:var_X; gs-bind-origin: reuse of vt_receiver_bindings args (ffl5 def-direct register origins T:/M:/S:/P:/RET:) at binds-attached sites (deduped against slot_param_groups.val_edges sites/pairs). Site->group attachment (both sound): (a) binds callee in group occ with matching slot (receiver-anchored binding, unique group per slot by construction); (b) mono slot: exactly one root among param groups of that slot (slot_anchor_v2 mono-only discipline; mono here = unique root among k-groups). Multi-site AND-merge per GS entity: CP purity = every scanned observation is a numeric immediate AND no occupant (occ member) has any CALL_ARG edge at (fn,k) in raw_constraints+supplementary (an edge without a classifiable G:<straddr> origin counts as non-immediate — conservative); SP purity = every observation is a string offset AND occupant CALL_ARG origins (when classifiable via callarg_origins) are all strings. Mixed evidence discarded. Equivalence edges are per-site independent (union).",
  "entity_format": {
   "gs": "GS:slot:k:root  (root 0x-prefixed upper hex; k=stack-arg index, this excluded)",
   "p": "P:FN:K           (upper hex no 0x)",
   "eax": "EAX:FN:site    (site = producer call insn addr, RETX-A convention)",
   "s": "S:FN:var_XX      (lower hex var name)"
  },
  "inputs": [
   "decompile-results/full_export/src/*.cpp (IDA disasm snapshot)",
   "anchors/slot_param_groups.json (groups + val_edges dedup baseline)",
   "anchors/vt_receiver_bindings.json (site->slot+callee+args reuse)",
   "anchors/param_usage_types_v2.json (edge dedup baseline)",
   "anchors/string_literals.json (string verification)",
   "tools/type_infer/constraints/raw_constraints.json + anchors/supplementary_call_args.json (occupant CALL_ARG purity check)",
   "anchors/callarg_origins.json (occupant-origin str refinement)",
   "D:\\RA2MD\\gamemd.exe (image VA range for address-valued immediates)"
  ],
